#: build-src/code/modules/workflow.md:1
msgid "The Workflow Module."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/code/modules/workflow.md:3
msgid ""
"In this module the primitive we operate on are workflows. In NumaHOP "
"workflows are tracking the life-cycle of document units."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/code/modules/workflow.md:6
msgid ""
"A workflow is constituted of states. Each states is either processed "
"automatically or require some user interaction in order to be processed. "
"Some states are process automatically and don't require much user "
"interaction such as the Diffusion, Archiving, Automatic Checks, or Delivery "
"Waiting."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/code/modules/workflow.md:11
msgid ""
"Once the condition required for the state to validate the workflow completes "
"it and start the next state. Some states can also be processed in parallel "
"such as diffusion and archiving states."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/code/modules/workflow.md:15
msgid ""
"The workflow is configured with a workflow model. The workflow model to use "
"on a document unit is configured either on the project, the lot, the train. "
"It can also be defined on the document unit itself. If a workflow model is "
"not present it will inherit the model of the parent document unit grouping. "
"(project -> lot \\-> train -> document unit)"
msgstr ""

